+## 0. How this contract is read — the Four Principles
+
+P1: evidence is judged by what could make the claim false, not by its existence. P2: every promise below names the runtime mechanism that must fire. P3: an unreachable control or unavailable production boundary is a finding, never a pass. P4: the probe suite prompts an independent auditor to break the product; it is not a finite definition of done.
+
+## 1. Target Launch Platforms
+
+The only reversible platform assumption supported by the workspace is a browser-based B2B UI. No host, delivery provider, database, or deployment configuration is yet selected; those are unresolved build decisions, not evidence.
+
+| Platform | Build artifact | Distribution |
+|---|---|---|
+| Web browser | Clean production web bundle, identified by commit SHA | Production web deployment (host not yet selected) |
+
+### 1a. Promise Proof Map
+
+| Promise | Claim | Observable mechanism | Admissible evidence | Failure probe |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| PRM-001 | No reminder is scheduled before explicit confirmation of action text, owner, and due date. | The scheduling write accepts only a server-validated confirmed action whose text, owner, and due date are all present; unconfirmed drafts have no schedule record. | `live-probe:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence/PRM-001-confirmation-rejection.md@58256ec` — real API/browser walk plus baselined datastore read-back as the acting workspace principal. | Submit each missing field; tamper a draft to `confirmed`; replay a stale confirmation. Any scheduled record or provider request makes the promise fail. |
+| PRM-002 | A workspace cannot read another workspace's transcript, action, or delivery status. | Every transcript, action, and delivery-status read is evaluated against the authenticated workspace boundary in the real datastore/API. | `live-probe:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence/PRM-002-cross-workspace-read.md@58256ec` — bidirectional live reads as two non-bypass workspace principals. | Seed data in workspace A, authenticate as workspace B, and attempt direct IDs, list/search endpoints, and delivery-status reads. Any returned A data makes the promise fail. |
+| PRM-003 | A confirmed reminder is delivered exactly once or exposes a truthful terminal failure state. | A durable delivery ledger atomically records one accepted delivery attempt per confirmed reminder; retries resolve to one delivered record or a terminal failed record visible to the owner. | `live-probe:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence/PRM-003-delivery-ledger.md@58256ec` and `db-catalog:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence/PRM-003-delivery-readback.md@58256ec` — real provider boundary plus pre/post datastore reads. | Force timeout after provider acceptance, duplicate queue messages, concurrent retries, and provider rejection. More than one delivery, no terminal state, or a success label after failure makes the promise fail. |
+
+## 2. Valid Proof Sources (per platform)
+
+### Platform: Web browser
+
+- A clean production bundle exercised at the deployed target with its real authentication, persistence, and delivery boundaries.
+- `ax-dump` plus `geometry` measurements from the running production-like bundle at 320px, 768px, and 1440px widths for the confirmation and delivery-status flows.
+- Baseline-before / read-back-after datastore evidence for any persistence claim.
+- A real provider acceptance/rejection observed at the provider boundary for the delivery claim.
+
+### 2a. Claim-type admissibility
+
+| Claim type | Admissible | Does not count |
+|---|---|---|
+| correctness | Tests, mutation guards, live probes, datastore reads, or static checks that can observe the stated invariant | A screenshot alone |
+| visibility | A live, bidirectional read as the actual allowed and denied workspace principals | Service-role/superuser reads, mocks, or endpoint-shaped 404s |
+| acceptance | Request issued to the deployed target or real service boundary | Mocked clients or hand-written fixtures without provenance |
+| persistence | Pre-walk baseline plus post-walk datastore read-back | Success UI or a post-walk read with no baseline |
+| fit | Baked-build AX tree plus measured container/content geometry at three widths | Rule-engine pass, props assertion, jsdom geometry, or unmeasured screenshot |
+| behaviour | Control-versus-treatment on the composed prompt with shipped model, if an AI behavior claim is added | Source-text assertion that a prompt rule exists |
+
+### 2b. Typed citations
+
+A typed citation has the form `<type>:<path>@<sha>`. The contract accepts only the following types: `test`, `mutation-guard`, `live-probe`, `db-catalog`, `ax-dump`, `geometry`, `capture`, `device-walk`, `model-eval`, and `static`.
+
+| Claim type | Discharge artifact | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| correctness | `test:path/to/suite@sha` | A correctness suite may discharge a correctness claim only. |
+| visibility | `live-probe:path/to/bidirectional-read@sha` | The denied and allowed principals must both be real. |
+| acceptance | `live-probe:path/to/real-boundary@sha` | The target must be deployed or the real engine. |
+| persistence | `db-catalog:path/to/baseline-and-readback@sha` | Both baseline and read-back are required. |
+| fit | `ax-dump:path/to/tree@sha` and `geometry:path/to/measurements@sha` | Both substrates are required. |
+| behaviour | `model-eval:path/to/control-treatment@sha` | Applies only if a generative behavior promise is added. |
+
+## 3. Invalid Proof Sources (anti-proof)
+
+- Dev-server screenshots or unadjudicated captures as launch proof.
+- Mock-only tests as proof that the deployed target, datastore authorization, or delivery provider accepts an interaction.
+- A service-role, superuser, or otherwise bypass-capable read as proof of workspace isolation.
+- A success screen as proof that a schedule or delivery record was persisted.
+- A single post-run database read with no baseline.
+- Tests passing as a readiness or ship claim.
+
+## 4. Required Runtime LARP / Integration Stress Tests
+
+| Test | Persona / principal | Pass condition | Evidence home |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Confirm a reviewed action | Facilitator in workspace A | Cold-start user can review action text, owner, and due date, explicitly confirm, and see one scheduled reminder; each incomplete confirmation is rejected without a schedule write. | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence/PRM-001-confirmation-rejection.md` |
+| Attempt cross-workspace access | Facilitators in workspaces A and B | A can read its own transcript/action/status; B cannot discover or read any of A's records through UI or direct request. | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence/PRM-002-cross-workspace-read.md` |
+| Deliver and recover a reminder | Facilitator in workspace A; real delivery provider | One confirmed reminder produces exactly one provider delivery, or a visible terminal failure state after bounded retries. | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence/PRM-003-delivery-ledger.md` |
+
+Each UI LARP must use a clean production bundle, cold start, runtime logs, AX dump, geometry measurements, and separately recorded DOES-IT-WORK and IS-IT-GOOD judgments. An inability to reach the confirmation or status surface is a P3 finding with a reproduced attempt log.
+
+## 5. Quality Judgment & Scoring Protocol
+
+Evidence makes a feature eligible for judgment; it does not make it good. Functional, emotional, social, trust, and commercial dimensions are scored 0–10 by an independent skeptical evaluator. A 9 requires a distinct dimension-specific skeptical note and no active P0/P1; a 10 additionally requires complete relevant runtime evidence and no active P2. Active P0/P1 caps a score at 4, active P2 caps it at 8, and a newer runtime contradiction immediately supersedes an older scorecard.
+
+## 6. Required Static Evidence
+
+Every UX-RC-or-higher report records the commit SHA, clean-build identifier, sanitized production configuration, primary-flow screenshots, browser accessibility tree, geometry measurements, browser logs with no unhandled errors, and network/backend traces for confirmation and delivery calls.
+
