+| speck:probe-library | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-citations.sh --check-probe-library specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence-contract.md` | manual | evidence | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/**` | `probe_classes>0` | — | — |
+
+## 7. Required Live-Service Evidence
+
+| Boundary | Required proof | Failure posture that must be observed |
+|---|---|---|
+| Authentication and workspace authorization | Two real workspace principals perform allowed and denied reads across transcript, action, and delivery status. | Missing/invalid identity is denied without leaking membership or records. |
+| Scheduling persistence | Baseline query, confirmation attempt, then datastore read-back of one schedule record. | Invalid confirmation leaves no schedule record. |
+| Delivery provider | Real acceptance and real forced rejection/timeout against the selected provider. | The system either records one delivery or exposes a truthful terminal failed state; it never silently hangs or reports success without evidence. |
+
+### PROFILE Gate Criteria
+
+No PROFILE claim is eligible until a production deployment and distribution are selected, the three promise rows have their required live evidence, and the UI LARPs are independently judged.
+
+## 8. Readiness Criteria
+
+| State | Required evidence | Blockers |
+|---|---|---|
+| NO-SHIP | Current state: no implementation or runtime evidence. | All promises lack live discharge. |
+| IMPL-GREEN | Relevant tests, types, lint, and a mutation check for each implemented guard. | Mock-only or skipped tests. |
+| INTEGRATION-GREEN | Real authorization, confirmation persistence, and delivery-provider round trips; live schema matches migrations. | Any unproven boundary or duplicate/ambiguous delivery outcome. |
