+| SHIP | Post-deploy smoke repeats the three promise probes against production. | Any production smoke mismatch. |
+
+## 9. Evidence Storage
+
+Evidence is stored under `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence/` using `<short-sha>-<promise>-<scenario>.<ext>`. UI captures, AX trees, geometry measurements, transcripts, network logs, and datastore read-backs are kept with the corresponding promise probe so a future evaluator can inspect the exact build and failure attempt.
+
+## 10. Who Can Mark a Gate Passed
+
+The agent may record automated correctness and live-boundary evidence. An independent auditor judges the adversarial probe results and the UI's FELT-GOOD/TASTE axes. A human owns release and any irreversible external delivery, production deployment, or charge.
+
+## 11. Adversarial Probe Suite
+
+| Probe | Expected behavior |
+|---|---|
+| Incomplete confirmation | Missing action text, owner, or due date is rejected and writes no schedule. |
+| Draft-state tampering | A client cannot schedule by changing an unconfirmed draft locally. |
+| Cross-workspace enumeration | Direct IDs, lists, search, and delivery-status calls reveal no other-workspace data. |
+| Duplicate delivery trigger | Concurrent/replayed queue messages produce one delivery ledger outcome, never duplicate user delivery. |
+| Provider timeout after acceptance | The final state is reconciled to delivered or terminal failure, never an indefinite/successful-looking ambiguity. |
+| Provider rejection/outage | Bounded retries end in a truthful user-visible terminal failure state. |
+| Missing auth header | The request is denied without a 500 or data leak. |
+| Oversized/malformed confirmation payload | Rejected without partial schedule or delivery writes. |
+| Evaluator-tampering scan | The change does not weaken test harnesses, CI, or evidence validators to manufacture a pass. |
+
