+## 12. Stale-Proof Policy
+
+Evidence is fresh only when it names a build SHA at HEAD or within seven days of commits and the proved artifact has not changed since collection. Evidence older than fourteen days or contradicted by newer runtime evidence cannot support readiness; rerun the relevant probe.
+
+## 13. Surrogate Proof Rule
+
+Any report using an invalid source is marked **Surrogate Proof**, cannot claim UX-RC or higher, links this contract's required proof, and creates a follow-up to collect the admissible substrate.
+
+## 14. LARP Runway & Efficiency Controls
+
+Every LARP records build SHA, browser/build identifier, and backend API fingerprint. Focused reruns may reuse a matching build during iteration, but UX-RC or higher requires a freshly compiled production bundle with incremental caches cleared.
